<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uttar Pradesh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uttar Pradesh is a state of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the most populous in the country, lying across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> plain with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucknow">Lucknow</a>. It contains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Varanasi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Prayagraj</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayodhya">Ayodhya</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mathura">Mathura</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>, and the Buddhist sites of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarnath">Sarnath</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushinagar">Kushinagar</a>. Formed under British rule as the United Provinces of Agra and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Oudh</a>, it took its present name in 1950.</p></div>
